MID_EV13_044_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_044_m01_001: I regret to say I don't have another warding chain\nhere for you.
MID_EV13_044_m01_002: I could try to craft one, but it requires a rare material.
MID_EV13_044_m01_003: It's found in very, very few places in Dagda. And\nthose places are...difficult to reach.
MID_EV13_044_m01_004: The only place I know where some can be found is\nthe forbidden land far to the northwest.
MID_EV13_044_m01_005: The forbidden land? You mean the sacred land of the\nPeople of the White Egg!
MID_EV13_044_m01_006: I happen to have a visitor from there right now.\nWait right here.
MID_EV13_044_m01_007: Here we are. This man has agreed to guide you\nto the forbidden land.
MID_EV13_044_m01_008: Hello. My name is Long—I hail from Kunlun. Pleased\nto meet you, Queen of Saramis and company.
MID_EV13_044_m01_009: <NCA>Ask about him.
MID_EV13_044_m01_010: <NCB>Ask about Kunlun.
MID_EV13_044_m01_011: <ACA>Truly? What sort of man are you? Are you of the\nWhite Egg as well?
MID_EV13_044_m01_012: <ACA>You are Long? Your name is well-known among the\nforest peoples as a master combatant.
MID_EV13_044_m01_013: <ACA>Yes, I am he. I come from the village of Kunlun—\nwhere the People of the White Egg reside.
MID_EV13_044_m01_014: <ACB>I am unfamiliar with Kunlun. Is that where the\nPeople of the White Egg live?
MID_EV13_044_m01_015: <ACB>In the ancient tongue, Kunlun means "sanctuary\nof the heavenly ones."
MID_EV13_044_m01_016: <ACB>It is my responsibility to periodically travel to the\noutside world, bringing news back to the village.
MID_EV13_044_m01_017: Then you are well suited to guide us there.\nThank you.
MID_EV13_044_m01_018: I also see that you carry one of the magic tubes\nwhich hurls lightning.
MID_EV13_044_m01_019: I met someone called Anatolia in Dagsion who\nused one just like it.
MID_EV13_044_m01_020: Anatolia? A good name. It means "land where the\nsun rises" in the ancient tongue.
MID_EV13_044_m01_021: Theodora, when you arrive in Kunlun, give this\nto a man named Zenon.
MID_EV13_044_m01_022: A written letter? The words seem different from\nthe writing in Dagda, but I cannot decipher them.
MID_EV13_044_m01_023: I mislike the written word. Yu Phas has forbidden\nthe practice since the long-ago days of Damascar.
MID_EV13_044_m01_024: Have you never wondered why Yu Phas might have\ngiven such an order?
MID_EV13_044_m01_025: Because writing is an evil that corrupts the human\nspirit. No?
MID_EV13_044_m01_026: No. It is because Dagda the Great feared the\nknowledge held by the People of the White Egg.
MID_EV13_044_m01_027: It was out of deference to him that Yu Phas forbade\nyour ancestors to read or write.
MID_EV13_044_m01_028: It was necessary so that Dagda would allow her to\nsave the lives of those children.
MID_EV13_044_m01_029: So long as Dagda the Great slumbers, there is no\nreason for the ban on written language.
MID_EV13_044_m01_030: Listen, Theodora. Writing is more precious than\nyou believe it to be.
MID_EV13_044_m01_031: Written language is how we learn about times\nother than our own.
MID_EV13_044_m01_032: Where your people came from, the mistakes they've\nmade... All of that valuable knowledge handed down.
MID_EV13_044_m01_033: It allows children to benefit from all of that.
MID_EV13_044_m01_034: I can share what I know while I live, but what\nabout after I'm gone?
MID_EV13_044_m01_035: I see no issue while Bonaventure is here. He is quick\nto educate me from his prodigious memory.
MID_EV13_044_m01_036: That is a short-sighted view. There are not many\nBonaventures in the world.
MID_EV13_044_m01_037: Besides, human memory is more fallible than you'd\nthink. We remember what we prefer.
MID_EV13_102_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_102_m01_001: Long, what sort of place is Kunlun?
MID_EV13_102_m01_002: Harsh, in a word.
MID_EV13_102_m01_003: The walls built by the temples confine its residents\nto the forbidden land.
MID_EV13_102_m01_004: There is insufficient water and food, hazardous\nweather, and deadly wildlife.
MID_EV13_102_m01_005: But the villagers persevere despite these hardships.\nThey live, hoping for a better world.
MID_EV13_102_m01_006: <NCA>Ask why they stay.
MID_EV13_102_m01_007: <NCB>Ask how he left.
MID_EV13_102_m01_008: <ACA>If life there is so harsh, why have they not tried\nto escape outside the walls?
MID_EV13_102_m01_009: <ACA>After all, you come and go as you please. It cannot\nbe so difficult.
MID_EV13_102_m01_010: <ACA>Oh, but it is. The exterior walls surrounding the land\nare monitored by people from the temples.
MID_EV13_102_m01_011: <ACA>Anyone discovered trying to climb the walls would\nbe captured instantly.
MID_EV13_102_m01_012: <ACA>I don't understand. Should we reach the forbidden\nland, how do you propose we get in?
MID_EV13_102_m01_013: You must have some method of coming and going\nfrom the outside world.
MID_EV13_102_m01_014: There is a secret underground passage built long,\nlong ago that the temples don't know about.
MID_EV13_102_m01_015: But the passage is dangerous. Only the most skilled\nare capable of making it through.
MID_EV13_102_m01_016: Sometimes, those who can't bear life in Kunlun any\nlonger attempt to escape.
MID_EV13_102_m01_017: Rarely, they succeed. Much more often, they perish\nin the attempt.
MID_EV13_102_m01_018: To save the people of Kunlun, we would need to\nopen Fezzan Gate, the way to the forbidden land.
MID_EV13_102_m01_019: Every year I visit those who managed to escape and\ngather information from them.
MID_EV13_102_m01_020: It is my duty to bring that news back to Kunlun.\nI have already returned once at the start of this year.
MID_EV13_102_m01_021: At that time, I brought a Mediator out with me\nand have been accompanying her ever since.
MID_EV13_102_m01_022: <NCA>Ask about Long's journey.
MID_EV13_102_m01_023: You mentioned a Mediator. I now recall Anatolia\nreferring to herself that way.
MID_EV13_102_m01_024: Precisely. She is the one I was escorting.
MID_EV13_102_m01_025: I was not planning to return to Kunlun so soon,\nbut I am doing so at Troy's request.
MID_EV13_102_m01_026: Rghh...
MID_EV13_102_m01_027: Are you alright?
MID_EV13_102_m01_028: I haven't yet recovered from the injuries I sustained\non my journey. Troy was tending them.
MID_EV13_102_m01_029: You agreed to guide us despite these wounds?\nI am truly grateful.
MID_EV13_102_m01_030: Have you known Troy for very long? The two of you\nseemed quite familiar with each other.
MID_EV13_102_m01_031: Troy was...a person of great importance early on in\nKunlun's history.
MID_EV13_102_m01_032: But she left the forbidden land to watch over the\nchildren that Yu Phas spared.
MID_EV13_102_m01_033: And now, her role is in providing support to your\npeople, as well as a handful of refugees from Kunlun.
MID_EV13_102_m01_034: I see. I never knew Troy went to such lengths\nfor us.
MID_EV13_045_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_045_m01_004: Long, was this also created by the People of the\nWhite Egg?
MID_EV13_045_m01_005: No. This is from a time long before Kunlun first\ndescended into this desert.
MID_EV13_045_m01_006: Our distant ancestors built it here. That was over\nthree thousand years ago now.
MID_EV13_045_m01_007: This desert was once home to a supermassive\nunderground facility called EX-061.
MID_EV13_045_m01_008: The Great Undoing of the past did not destroy it\nentirely. Some of it still functions today.
MID_EV13_045_m01_009: This passage is part of that facility. The paths to the\ndeepest levels are blocked, however.
MID_EV13_045_m01_010: Though an entrance leading deeper inside may\nexist somewhere in the desert.
MID_EV13_045_m01_011: I know it's part of the job, but...I really, really don't\nwanna poke my nose in there.
MID_EV13_045_m01_012: Though maybe if I got a bump in pay, I could\nthink about it.
MID_EV13_045_m01_013: <NCA>Consider the request.
MID_EV13_045_m01_014: That depends on the effort put in. I shall always\ncompensate work well done.
MID_EV13_045_m01_015: In that case, I'm your gal.
MID_EV13_045_m01_016: This passage will take us inside the walls without\nusing the gate.
MID_EV13_045_m01_017: I'm impressed you found a way around the temples'\nsurveillance. It's good for us.
MID_EV13_045_m01_018: I wasn't expecting it to be so pleasant in here. It's\ncertainly a stark difference from the desert.
MID_EV13_045_m01_019: True, but that can be a problem in itself.
MID_EV13_045_m01_020: It's as comfortable for desert creatures as it is for us,\nand some of them can be very dangerous.
MID_EV13_045_m01_021: They like to build their nests here. How safe our\njourney is depends on...
MID_EV13_045_m01_022: Aah! What was that?!
MID_EV13_045_m01_023: ...our luck and skill.
MID_EV13_045_m01_024: I will protect you as best I can, but I may not be\nable to handle all of them.
MID_EV13_045_m01_025: If you are capable of defending yourselves, I suggest\nyou do so.
MID_EV13_045_m01_026: Hmph. The warriors of Saramis are unmatched.\nWorry not on our account.
MID_EV13_046_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_046_m01_001: So this is it... The White Egg.
MID_EV13_046_m01_002: It sure is! It's big, round, white, and totally\ncracked open.
MID_EV13_046_m01_003: The legendary White Egg is even grander than\nI had envisioned...
MID_EV13_046_m01_004: I struggle to believe that any human, let alone our\nancestors, could create something so magnificent.
MID_EV13_046_m01_005: Welcome, Queen of Saramis, ruler of our\nlong-lost kin.
MID_EV13_046_m01_006: Your homecoming cannot have been easy.\nKunlun welcomes you.
MID_EV13_046_m01_007: I am Zenon, leader of this village.
MID_EV13_046_m01_008: A pleasure. But first, I have something for you\npassed along from Troy.
MID_EV13_046_m01_009: Thank you. Pardon me while I give this a quick skim.
MID_EV13_046_m01_010: So you need a warding chain, do you? Making one\nisn't so hard.
MID_EV13_046_m01_011: Truly?! That is excellent news!
MID_EV13_046_m01_012: The problem is that I'd need a special material to\ncraft it.
MID_EV13_046_m01_013: It's a unique metal called epimenium. It has a curious\nability to interfere with the human mind.
MID_EV13_046_m01_014: If I lend you a sensor, would you mind searching for\nsome around the northern passage?
MID_EV13_046_m01_015: <NCA>Accept his offer.
MID_EV13_046_m01_016: Absolutely. We will do whatever we must to retrieve\nthe material for you.
MID_EV13_046_m01_017: Ah!
MID_EV13_046_m01_018: Something the matter, boss? You seem jittery.
MID_EV13_046_m01_019: Our host referred to our "homecoming" before. I had\nnot fully considered it.
MID_EV13_046_m01_020: My ancestors here were prisoners of war, who owe\ntheir lives to Yu Phas's grace.
MID_EV13_046_m01_021: After a long journey, they established the kingdom of\nDamascar. We have inherited their dreams.
MID_EV13_046_m01_022: And now, nearly one thousand years later, we return\nto where it all began.
MID_EV13_046_m01_023: To see the White Egg with my own eyes...
MID_EV13_046_m01_024: I am struck with the knowledge that the stories Troy\ntold me in my youth were true ones.
MID_EV13_046_m01_025: Dagda feared us. So he razed it all.
MID_EV13_046_m01_026: The Great Undoing... The war between our ancestors\nand the gods.
MID_EV13_046_m01_027: That titanic clash destroyed the world until the gods\nguided its slow rebirth.
MID_EV13_046_m01_028: But they feared it would all happen again, so they\nattempted to bury our ways.
MID_EV13_046_m01_029: Know this, Zenon. I trust no god nor temple save\nfor Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_046_m01_030: If my Saramis is ever targeted for tragedy in the way\nthat Damascar once was...
MID_EV13_046_m01_031: I mean to resist them with all that I am. And I ask\nthat you aid me in this.
MID_EV13_046_m01_032: Should that day come, look to our Mediator. You will\nfind none left in Kunlun capable of helping you.
MID_EV13_046_m01_033: You mean Anatolia? She did say I was "selected for\nher protection," now that I think on it.
MID_EV13_046_m01_034: Indeed. She, Troy, and Long will be staunch allies,\nshould worse come to worst.
MID_EV13_047_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_047_m01_001: Thank you for waiting. One new warding chain,\nmade just for you.
MID_EV13_047_m01_002: I owe you and your people a great debt. If you are\never in danger, you can call upon Saramis.
MID_EV13_047_m01_003: In Kunlun's hour of need, Saramis will repay her\ndebt in force.
MID_EV13_047_m01_004: Besides, we are like long-lost family. We are your\nnatural allies irrespective of debts.
MID_EV13_047_m01_005: That is kind of you. I'll tell the villagers, and Long\nwill let those of us in the outside world know.
MID_EV13_047_m01_006: Queen Theodora...there is something else you\nshould know.
MID_EV13_047_m01_007: Troy's letter contained a fragment of the broken\nwarding chain.
MID_EV13_047_m01_008: I analyzed it and was surprised to find it was far\nmore frayed than I expected.
MID_EV13_047_m01_009: There is a will lingering inside that arm—or maybe\nI should call it a hatred.
MID_EV13_047_m01_010: And its power is far beyond what the chain is\ncapable of suppressing.
MID_EV13_047_m01_011: The warding chain is a crystallization of our wisdom,\nbut it can't stand up to such concentrated evil.
MID_EV13_047_m01_012: Not for long, anyway. I regret to say I don't have\na permanent solution for you.
MID_EV13_047_m01_013: <NCA>Feign unconcern.
MID_EV13_047_m01_014: If it lasts the duration of the Heroic Games, that\nshall be time enough.
MID_EV13_047_m01_015: Our victory there will assure fulfillment of the long-\nheld dream of Saramis.
MID_EV13_047_m01_016: If I can achieve that, it matters little what becomes\nof me after.
MID_EV13_047_m01_017: Hey, Queen Theodora? Can you cool it with that\ntalk already?
MID_EV13_047_m01_018: What did you say to me?
MID_EV13_047_m01_019: I've been thinking for a while that you're carrying\ntoo heavy a load for one woman.
MID_EV13_047_m01_020: I can't imagine having to shoulder a whole kingdom's\ndreams. I think I'd quit immediately.
MID_EV13_047_m01_021: So don't go looking forward to a tragic end as soon\nas the games are over.
MID_EV13_047_m01_022: Wouldn't it be better to find a way to live even\nlonger and do even more?
MID_EV13_047_m01_023: The people love you, Queen Theodora. Even I don't\nactually hate you.
MID_EV13_047_m01_024: You said it, Lil. The boss takes too much of the\nstrain on herself!
MID_EV13_047_m01_025: There's gotta be some way out. Let Bona sleep on\nit, and he's bound to come up with something!
MID_EV13_047_m01_026: Indeed. I will devote myself utterly toward tackling\nthe problem.
MID_EV13_047_m01_027: So will I! So will all of us. Anything we can do for\nyou, we will do gladly!
MID_EV13_047_m01_028: You are the last of my subjects I expected to hear\nsuch sentiments from, Lilian.
MID_EV13_047_m01_029: Ah, Queen Theodora. May we all be blessed with\nsuch meddlesome friends.